    "senderName": "NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "headline": "Flood Warning issued November 13 at 7:24PM MST until November 17 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by upstream dam release continues.\n\n* WHERE...Maricopa County in south central Arizona...\nNortheastern Yuma County in southwestern Arizona...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MST Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is expected. Low-water crossings are\nlikely to become inundated with water and may not be passable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 724 PM MST, water releases from Painted Rock Dam continue with\nflow peaking at 3000 cfs. A streamflow gauge immediately\ndownstream  also indicated a stage of 9.93 feet.\n- Flooding is expected along the Gila River.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFarmlands and low-water crossings along the Gila River.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
    "response": "Avoid",
